      "proof_trace": "`float::int_div(collateral_amount, exchange_rate)` performs floor integer division; when `exchange_rate > collateral_amount` (in decimal terms), the result is 0. The only guard is `assert!(collateral_amount > 0)` at line 157, but there is no post-computation `assert!(mint_amount > 0)`. `deposit_underlying(coin)` consumes the user's coin before the zero cToken balance is returned, causing permanent fund loss. The TODO comment at line 159 explicitly acknowledges this rounding risk without mitigation.",
      "attack_scenario": "In a mature pool where exchange_rate > 1.0 (normal after any interest accrual), an attacker or honest user calls `deposit` with `collateral_amount` less than the current exchange_rate in raw token units; `mint_amount = 0` is computed, the deposited coin is transferred to the reserve, and 0 cTokens are returned \u2014 the user loses their deposit while all existing cToken holders benefit.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-01b-partial1-inv-005"
    },
    "text": "Mint operation must produce mint_amount > 0 when coin.value > 0.",
    "assertion": "coin.value > 0 => mint_amount = coin.value / exchange_rate > 0",
    "covers": "SG-001",
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "type": "invariant"
  }
}

